{
  "schema": "ancora.parity.scenario.v1",
  "id": "s05-shared-teacher-continuation",
  "title": "Two specialties of one plan share a teacher in one period; the legacy window's default options; the same scope requested twice",
  "notes": [
    "Characterization for #95 (D7, D11). Run F places the other specialty's activity with the shared teacher T first. Run E1 then cannot use T's cell: legacy reads the teacher's occupancy in the same period (valor_restriccion_profesor, the teacher load at generar.sql:869).",
    "Runs F and E1 use the options the legacy generator window posts by default (ancoragoh_client_wins_generador.js: forma 1, compactar 1, parche and parche1 false, buscalugar true; D11). Run E2 repeats the E scope with the options Drupal sends by default (compactar 0, buscalugar false).",
    "Legacy continuation (PAR-085): run E2 finds every E demand placed and adds nothing. The Drupal worker deletes the scope's placements first (D7) and places them again; with these records the cells come out the same, so the end state is identical on both sides.",
    "The metrics count every placement of the period (tst.metrics: placed = distinct template and group in the period), so E1 and E2 report placed=2 for one demand."
  ],
  "users": [
    {"key": "admin", "name": "Administrator", "legacy": "seeded-admin"},
    {"key": "alice", "name": "Alice Planner"}
  ],
